#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# catalan

#% text
# `catalan` is Catalan's constant `G = 0.9159...`, the sum of `(-1)^k/(2k + 1)^2` for `k >= 0`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `catalan` is exact and known to be a positive real; `n(catalan, d)` gives `d` digits.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
catalan
#% output
#= catalan

#% cell
n(catalan)
#% output
#= 0.915965594177219

#% cell
n(catalan, 40)
#% output
#= 0.9159655941772190150546035149323841107741494

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The alternating series:

#% cell
sum((-1)^k/(2*k + 1.0)^2, [k, 0, 10000]) - n(catalan)
#% output
#= 1.2497500812003182e-9

#% text
# An integral of `atan(x)/x`:

#% cell
n_integrate(atan(x)/x, [x, 0, 1]) - n(catalan)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `pi`, `euler_gamma`, `catalan_number`, `zeta`
